WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.510
- [Instructor] In this video,
we're going to talk about

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:06.900
how people can interact with, influence,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.910
and participate in society.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.370
When you do so, you're
participating in civic life,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.490
which is distinct from your private life.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:21.960
Private life includes all the
ways that you pursue happiness

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.720
through relationships,
hobbies, or your job,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.020
that is, if you're not
a member of government.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.300
Civic life includes all the
ways that you might take part

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.280
in solving the problems of your community,

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.750
whether that's by
volunteering in civil society,

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:45.750
making rules or laws, or
serving in a government body,

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.523
whether that's the school
council or the U.S. Senate.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.030
So if you like playing video games,

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.270
playing for fun is part
of your private life.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.240
But if you joined a group petitioning

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.810
for more representation

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.410
of diverse characters in video games,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.330
you'd be entering into civic life.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.900
Then you're not just doing things

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.420
that make you happy individually.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.440
You're striving to have an
effect on the lives of others.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.620
So when you step into civic life,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.170
you will become involved
with politics and government.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.960
Although you often hear
them lumped together,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.540
they're not actually the same thing.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.570
You could say that politics is something

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.300
that you do, an action.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.930
Politics encompasses all the ways

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.850
that people reach agreements in a group,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.740
by negotiating, compromising, or voting.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.900
And those people might
not agree with each other,

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.660
but through the political process,

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.990
they agree to be bound by the rules

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.680
that they've negotiated together.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.910
So in the large scale,

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:57.240
politics describes both
how Congress debates bills

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.700
and how you and your brother
decide who does the dishes.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.630
Then there's government.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.720
Government is a noun,

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.550
and it describes both the institutions

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.960
like the Supreme Court or the city council

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.110
which make and enforce laws,

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.110
as well as the people who
serve in those institutions.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:23.590
So government could describe both FIFA,

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.750
the international
governing body for soccer,

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.210
as well as the referee whose
job it is to enforce the rules

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.520
that soccer teams and
players agree to abide by.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.730
Okay, so now that you've
learned about civic life,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:43.730
private life, politics, and
government, here's a pop quiz.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.680
I'm gonna give you a few scenarios,

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.920
and you see if you can match
them to the correct term.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.020
First up, Ayla's church
provides food and shelter

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.410
for the homeless community
during the winter

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.130
to keep them out of the cold.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:02.940
Is this an example of
civic life, private life,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.500
politics, or government?

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.690
Pause the video here
and see what you think.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:12.160
If you guessed civic life, you're correct.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.410
Ayla is participating in what
we call civil society here,

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.720
which you might remember
from another video.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.170
Civil society includes all
of the voluntary institutions

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:24.860
that people form and join

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.700
outside of government and the market.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.600
She's doing something for her community.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.250
Okay, next.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.570
The Supreme Court hears a case

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:38.600
about internet copyright
law and the First Amendment.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:43.180
Is this an example of
civic life, private life,

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.010
politics, or government?

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.640
This is government.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.740
The Supreme Court is
part of a governing body

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.410
that enforces the rules.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.120
Okay, last one.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.580
Jeffrey, a representative for the AARP,

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.540
reaches out to Senator Rodriguez
to provide more information

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.900
on the impact a bill making its way

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.980
through the House will
have on senior citizens.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.740
He wants to secure Senator
Rodriguez's support

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.890
when the bill reaches the Senate.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:17.840
Is this an example of
civic life, private life,

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.560
politics, or government?

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.210
If you guessed politics, you're right.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.720
Jeffrey is providing information,

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.930
hoping to influence a decision
that will affect others.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.460
Okay, thanks for playing.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.933
Keep practicing your skills in
the exercise for this lesson.

